      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NASTY (5) resumes. His only run to date was in a good Inglis race during Cup week at Flemington, well in the market there but copping some tough conditions and struggling. Since gelded, he's jumped out well and can do much better. MIRADOR (8) has had two runs back in solid company over 1000m. She looks like she'll appreciate rising in trip now and should be at peak fitness. Hard to hold out. ARTISON (6) ran well first here despite being sent out a $21 chance, working home well to grab second. Better for that and comes under notice now. LIQUID ASSET (4) was sound here on debut over 1100m when in the market and can improve while INSIDE WORD (3) was poor on slow ground at Swan Hill as favourite on debut but can do much better.",
